 {"id":"moon-2017-07-31","title":"The Eight-Day Moon","target":"moon","session":null,"captured":"2017-07-31","processed":"2017-07-31","revision":"v1","supersedes":null,"acquisition":{"scope":"Questar 3.5\" (prime focus)","sensor":"Raspberry Pi Camera Module v2","sensor_temp_c":null,"filter":"none","exposure":null,"integration":null,"integration_bucket":"under1h","location":"Raleigh area, North Carolina","moon":null,"coordinates":"Az 226° 11′ SW · Alt +25° 50′ · RA 15h 35m 51.1s · Dec −14° 40′ 07″ · HA 02h 48m 45s W","processing":["50-panel mosaic in Microsoft ICE"]},"classification":{"object_type":"solar system","sub_kind":"Moon","catalogs":[],"constellation":"Libra","is_event":false,"event_type":null,"tags":["moon","mosaic"]},"media":{"thumb":"media/moon-2017-07-31/thumb.jpg","web":"media/moon-2017-07-31/web.jpg","full":"media/moon-2017-07-31/full.jpg"},"body_html":"<p>A 50-panel mosaic of the eight-day-old waxing gibbous Moon, taken at the prime focus of a Questar 3.5-inch telescope with a Raspberry Pi Camera Module v2 and stitched in Microsoft ICE.\n\nPosition at capture — azimuth 226° 11′ 18.9″ (southwest), altitude +25° 50′ 10.4″; right ascension 15h 35m 51.10s, declination −14° 40′ 07.3″; hour angle 02h 48m 45.22s W; ecliptic longitude/latitude 235° 11′ 11.2″ / +04° 31′ 05.6″; galactic longitude/latitude 351° 31′ 28.9″ / +32° 25′ 53.8″.</p>","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0"},
